=== description and row shapes ===
  column names: ['id', 'title']
  id is NUMBER: True, title is STRING: True
  fetchone():   (1, 'deploy')
  as a dict:    {'id': 2, 'title': 'rollback'}
  fetchmany(5): [(3, 'audit')] (only the rows that are left)
  fetchall():   [] (result exhausted)
  iterating:    ['deploy', 'rollback', 'audit']

=== CLOB column ===
  fetched as: dict with a 'lob_type' key: True
  a NULL CLOB is: None
  CAST(body AS VARCHAR): 'rolled out'

=== Database errors: class, errno, sqlstate, args ===
  duplicate key -> IntegrityError
    errno=-670 code=-670 sqlstate='23000'
    len(args)=1, args[0] is the message: True
  unknown table -> ProgrammingError, errno=-493
  syntax error  -> ProgrammingError, errno=-493

=== Interface errors: no database round trip ===
  closed cursor -> InterfaceError (Cursor is closed), has errno: False
  InterfaceError is a DatabaseError: False
  InterfaceError is a pycubrid.Error: True

Dropped cookbook_cdb_events
